      "obligations": ["VIII-2", "VII-4", "VII-14"],
      "derivation": "Seq 8 a second time is silence. This envelope carries a different return padlock from every other in this scenario, which is what makes the refresh rule observable: Article XII refreshes the way back between the seq and the leash, \"not earlier, because a replayed message would otherwise rewrite a live way back with a retired one.\" The row must still hold the padlock it learned, not the one this replay carried. This is also Article VII's \"one voice is used from one place\": two machines sharing a voice keep two counters, and the second to spend a number is silently refused — which is exactly this exchange, the two senders being indistinguishable at the door by design.",
